#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:14
msgid "Abstract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:16
msgid ""
"Introduce a standard format for a static description file with build details "
"of Python installations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:21
msgid "Rationale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:23
msgid ""
"When introspecting a Python installation, running code is often undesirable "
"or impossible. Having a static description file makes various of Python "
"build details available without having to run the interpreter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:27
msgid ""
"This is helpful for use-cases such as cross-compilation, Python launchers, "
"etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:31
msgid "Scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:33
msgid ""
"This PEP defines a format for the description file, and a standard location "
"for where to place it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:38
msgid "Location"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:40
msgid ""
"When possible, Python installations should install the static description "
"file inside the standard library directory, with the name ``build-details."
"json`` (Eg. ``/usr/lib/python3.14/build-details.json``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:47
msgid ""
"Given that there may be technical challenges, Python implementations are not "
"required to provide the file if not feasable. In such scenarios, they may "
"choose to provide it in a different maner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0739.rst:54
msgid ""
"Notwithstanding the standard location specified here, it does not prevent "
"the file from **additionally** being provided in another location, and with "
"a different name. In fact, the PEP authors expect future PEPs to define "
"additional locations to install this file, for better discoverability."
msgstr ""

